PLACEHOLDER — no licence has been chosen yet.

This file intentionally does NOT contain a licence. Delete it and replace it
with the real licence text once you have decided.

Common choices for research code:

  * MIT           - shortest permissive licence; allows reuse in closed products.
                    Widely used for academic code releases.
  * Apache-2.0    - permissive, like MIT, but also grants an explicit patent
                    licence and requires stating changes. A good fit here because
                    parts of this repository are already Apache-2.0
                    (see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md), which keeps everything
                    under one licence family.
  * BSD-3-Clause  - permissive, similar to MIT with a no-endorsement clause.

Before you publish, also check THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md: the eight comparison-method
directories under model/ each come from a different upstream project, and some of
them may not permit redistribution. Confirm their terms, or remove those
directories and link to the original repositories in the README instead.
